---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Brand standards"
  description="Hypertext Studio brand assets, typography, colors, writing, and product attribution."
>
  <article class="brand-guide">
    <header class="guide-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Hypertext Studio</p>
      <h1 id="brand-standards">
        <a class="heading-link" href="#brand-standards"
          ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Brand standards</a
        >
      </h1>
      <p class="guide-lede">
        Identity, assets, and usage for studio communications and product credits.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="identity">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h2 id="identity">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#identity" title="Link to Brand overview"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Brand overview</a
          >
        </h2><p>The studio name, statement, and character.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <h3 id="studio-statement">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#studio-statement"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Studio statement</a
          >
        </h3>
        <figure class="example statement-example">
          <blockquote>Hypertext Studio builds software for humans.</blockquote><figcaption>
            Primary studio statement
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Hypertext Studio is a software studio behind Docket, LogDate, and Curfew.</p>
        <h3 id="name">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#name"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Name and address</a
          >
        </h3>
        <dl class="name-grid">
          <div><dt>Company name</dt><dd>Hypertext Studio</dd></div><div>
            <dt>Website address</dt><dd class="mono">hypertext.studio</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          Use the full company name on first mention. After that, “the studio” is a natural
          reference.
        </p>
        <h3 id="brand-character">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#brand-character"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Brand character</a
          >
        </h3>
        <p>
          Clear, thoughtful, and curious. Express the connection to hypertext through readable
          information, useful links, and visible destinations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="marks">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h2 id="marks">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#marks" title="Link to Logo"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Logo</a
          >
        </h2><p>The wordmark, compact symbol, and their use.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <p class="section-intro">
          Use the supplied logo artwork. Choose the variant that remains clear against its
          background.
        </p><h3 id="wordmark">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#wordmark" title="Link to Wordmark"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Wordmark</a
          >
        </h3><div class="grid">
          <figure class="example">
            <img
              class="mark"
              src="/brand/wordmark.svg"
              alt="Hypertext Studio wordmark in Ink"
            /><figcaption class="example-caption">
              <span>Light backgrounds</span><a href="/brand/wordmark.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
            </figcaption>
          </figure><figure class="example dark">
            <img
              class="mark"
              src="/brand/wordmark-paper.svg"
              alt="Hypertext Studio wordmark in Light Ink"
            /><figcaption class="example-caption">
              <span>Dark backgrounds</span><a href="/brand/wordmark-paper.svg" download
                >Download SVG</a
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div><table class="table specs">
          <tbody
            ><tr><th scope="row">Typeface</th><td>IBM Plex Mono Regular, weight 400</td></tr><tr
              ><th scope="row">Tracking</th><td>−0.03em</td></tr
            ><tr
              ><th scope="row">Clear space</th><td>At least one lowercase x-height on each side</td
              ></tr
            ><tr><th scope="row">Minimum digital width</th><td>160 px</td></tr></tbody
          >
        </table><h3 id="symbol">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#symbol" title="Link to Compact symbol"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Compact symbol</a
          >
        </h3><div class="symbol-example">
          <img src="/favicon.svg" alt="Hypertext Studio angle-bracket symbol" /><div>
            <p>
              Use the angle brackets for favicons, avatars, and small placements. Keep a readable
              studio name nearby when context is needed.
            </p><div class="symbol-sizes">
              <figure>
                <img src="/favicon.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="16 pixel symbol" /><figcaption>
                  16 px
                </figcaption>
              </figure><figure>
                <img src="/favicon.svg" width="24" height="24" alt="24 pixel symbol" /><figcaption>
                  24 px
                </figcaption>
              </figure><figure>
                <img src="/favicon.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="32 pixel symbol" /><figcaption>
                  32 px
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div><p class="caption">
              <a href="/favicon.svg" download="hypertext-studio-symbol.svg">Download symbol SVG</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div><h3 id="usage">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#usage" title="Link to Logo usage"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Logo usage</a
          >
        </h3><ul>
          <li>Keep the lowercase name, hyphen, and brackets together on one line.</li><li>
            Preserve the artwork's proportions and leave clear space around it.
          </li><li>Use a clear background and keep product accents out of the studio mark.</li><li>
            Use the plain studio name when space cannot accommodate the full wordmark.
          </li>
        </ul><p class="caption">
          The closing form, <code>&lt;/hypertext-studio&gt;</code>, can end a page or document after
          the primary name or wordmark has appeared.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="typography">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h2 id="typography">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#typography" title="Link to Typography"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Typography</a
          >
        </h2><p>Font families and a practical reading hierarchy.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <p class="section-intro">
          Inter is the default family. Use IBM Plex Mono for the wordmark, addresses, references,
          and code.
        </p><h3 id="font-roles">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#font-roles" title="Link to Font roles"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Font roles</a
          >
        </h3><div class="font-row">
          <div>
            <strong>Inter</strong><p class="family-use">
              Headings, prose, navigation, and credits.
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <p class="font-sample">Readable information.</p><p class="family-use">
              400 body · 500–600 headings · 600 emphasis
            </p>
          </div>
        </div><div class="font-row">
          <div>
            <strong>IBM Plex Mono</strong><p class="family-use">
              Wordmark, addresses, references, and code.
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <p class="font-sample plex-sample">hypertext.studio</p><p class="family-use">
              400 Regular
            </p>
          </div>
        </div><h3 id="type-scale">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#type-scale" title="Link to Type scale"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Type scale</a
          >
        </h3><p>
          Use this starting hierarchy for digital studio materials. Adapt the scale to the medium
          and available space.
        </p><table class="table">
          <thead
            ><tr
              ><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Size</th><th scope="col">Line height</th
              ></tr
            ></thead
          ><tbody
            ><tr><td>Display</td><td>48–96 px</td><td>1.05</td></tr><tr
              ><td>Page title</td><td>32 px</td><td>1.15</td></tr
            ><tr><td>Section heading</td><td>24 px</td><td>1.25</td></tr><tr
              ><td>Body</td><td>16–18 px</td><td>1.5–1.6</td></tr
            ><tr><td>Caption or credit</td><td>14–16 px</td><td>1.5</td></tr><tr
              ><td>Address or reference</td><td>13–14 px</td><td>1.5</td></tr
            ></tbody
          >
        </table><p class="caption">
          Use sentence case for headings. Keep body paragraphs around 55–75 characters per line.
          Establish hierarchy through size, weight, and space.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="palette">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h2 id="palette">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#palette" title="Link to Color palette"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Color palette</a
          >
        </h2><p>Core neutrals and supporting interface colors.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <p class="section-intro">
          Warm neutrals carry the studio identity. Blue identifies interactions. Keep a product's
          accent with that product.
        </p><h3 id="primary-colors">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#primary-colors" title="Link to Primary colors"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Primary colors</a
          >
        </h3><div class="colors">
          <figure>
            <div class="swatch" style="background:#fbfbfa"></div><figcaption>
              <strong>Paper</strong><span class="mono">#FBFBFA</span><span class="muted"
                >Light background</span
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure><figure>
            <div class="swatch" style="background:#25231f"></div><figcaption>
              <strong>Ink</strong><span class="mono">#25231F</span><span class="muted"
                >Text on light</span
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure><figure>
            <div class="swatch" style="background:#181713"></div><figcaption>
              <strong>Dark Paper</strong><span class="mono">#181713</span><span class="muted"
                >Dark background</span
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure><figure>
            <div class="swatch" style="background:#f3f3ed"></div><figcaption>
              <strong>Light Ink</strong><span class="mono">#F3F3ED</span><span class="muted"
                >Text on dark</span
              >
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div><h3 id="supporting-colors">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#supporting-colors" title="Link to Supporting colors"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Supporting colors</a
          >
        </h3><table class="table">
          <thead
            ><tr><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr
            ></thead
          ><tbody
            ><tr
              ><td>Secondary text</td><td class="mono">#666666</td><td class="mono">#AAA99F</td></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Supporting surface</td><td class="mono">#F1F2EE</td><td class="mono">#1A1B17</td
              ></tr
            ><tr><td>Divider</td><td class="mono">#DDDDDA</td><td class="mono">#373832</td></tr><tr
              ><td>Links and focus</td><td class="mono">#1646D8</td><td class="mono">#91ADFF</td
              ></tr
            ></tbody
          >
        </table><h3 id="contrast-and-links">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#contrast-and-links" title="Link to Contrast and links"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Contrast and links</a
          >
        </h3><ul>
          <li>Keep ordinary text contrast at least 4.5:1 against its background.</li><li>
            Underline inline text links. Heading links reveal a hash on hover or focus.
          </li><li>
            Use a readable label or other clear cue for essential information; subtle dividers and
            surfaces organize content.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="composition">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span><h2 id="composition">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#composition" title="Link to Imagery and layout"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Imagery and layout</a
          >
        </h2><p>Composition, product imagery, and motion.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <p class="section-intro">
          Give each composition a clear subject. Use real product material and organize it through
          alignment, hierarchy, and space.
        </p><h3 id="layout">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#layout" title="Link to Layout"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Layout</a
          >
        </h3><figure>
          <div class="example composition">
            <img class="mark" src="/brand/wordmark.svg" alt="Hypertext Studio" /><div
              class="composition-grid"
            >
              <p class="composition-title">Hypertext Studio builds software for humans.</p><aside
                class="composition-reference"
              >
                <p>Applications from Hypertext Studio.</p><a
                  class="mono"
                  href="https://hypertext.studio/#products">hypertext.studio/#products</a
                >
              </aside>
            </div>
          </div><figcaption class="caption">
            Studio announcement: wordmark, subject, and a useful destination.
          </figcaption>
        </figure><ul>
          <li>Align related information and give the main subject the strongest emphasis.</li><li>
            Add an annotation when it helps explain the subject.
          </li><li>
            Use an 8 px spacing rhythm, with 4 px for small adjustments. Set margins to suit the
            medium.
          </li>
        </ul><h3 id="imagery">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#imagery" title="Link to Imagery"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Imagery</a
          >
        </h3><ul>
          <li>Use real product assets and legible screenshots.</li><li>
            Use ASCII illustration for recognizable subjects.
          </li><li>
            Keep decorative artwork separate from readable text. Describe images that carry
            information.
          </li>
        </ul><h3 id="motion">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#motion" title="Link to Motion"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Motion</a
          >
        </h3><p>
          Use motion to clarify transitions and responses. Preserve information in a static version
          and respect reduced-motion settings.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="voice">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span><h2 id="voice">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#voice" title="Link to Voice and tone"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Voice and tone</a
          >
        </h2><p>How the studio speaks and writes.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <p class="section-intro">
          Write clearly and directly. Say what the studio or product does, using concrete language
          and claims supported by the software.
        </p><h3 id="writing-rules">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#writing-rules" title="Link to Writing rules"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Writing rules</a
          >
        </h3><ul>
          <li>Use “we” when the studio speaks.</li><li>
            Use the company name when another organization or product describes it.
          </li><li>Address the reader as “you” when it makes an explanation clearer.</li><li>
            Explain privacy and reliability through specific behavior. Avoid unsupported
            superlatives and promises.
          </li>
        </ul><h3 id="writing-examples">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#writing-examples" title="Link to Examples"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Examples</a
          >
        </h3><table class="table">
          <thead
            ><tr><th scope="col" style="width:25%">Context</th><th scope="col">Wording</th></tr
            ></thead
          ><tbody
            ><tr><td>Studio statement</td><td>Hypertext Studio builds software for humans.</td></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Company description</td><td
                >Hypertext Studio is a software studio behind Docket, LogDate, and Curfew.</td
              ></tr
            ><tr><td>Support</td><td>Email hello@hypertext.studio for help.</td></tr><tr
              ><td>Unavailable page</td><td>There's no page at this address.</td></tr
            ></tbody
          >
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="attribution">
      <header class="chapter-heading">
        <span class="chapter-number" aria-hidden="true">07</span><h2 id="attribution">
          <a class="heading-link" href="#attribution" title="Link to Product attribution"
            ><span class="heading-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span>Product attribution</a
          >
        </h2><p>A consistent connection between products and the studio.</p>
      </header><div class="chapter-content">
        <p class="section-intro">
          Use a supporting credit to connect a product to Hypertext Studio. Keep the product name
          primary and use the application's own typeface and text color.
        </p><div class="grid">
          <div class="example">
            <p class="credit-label">Default credit</p><p class="credit-name">LogDate</p><p
              class="credit"
            >
              Made by <a href="https://hypertext.studio">Hypertext Studio</a>
            </p>
          </div><div class="example">
            <p class="credit-label">Compact credit</p><p class="credit-name">LogDate</p><p
              class="credit"
            >
              by <a href="https://hypertext.studio">Hypertext Studio</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div><ul>
          <li>Link the studio name to hypertext.studio.</li><li>
            Match the surrounding supporting text size, normally at least 14 px.
          </li><li>In descriptive prose, use “A product of Hypertext Studio.”</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .brand-guide {
    max-inline-size: 80rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem) var(--layout-margin) 5rem;
  }
  .guide-intro {
    padding-block-end: 3.5rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }
  .guide-intro h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }
  .guide-lede {
    max-inline-size: 45ch;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
  .brand-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 4rem;
    border-block-start: var(--rule-thin);
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }
  .chapter-heading {
    position: sticky;
    inset-block-start: calc(var(--header-block-size) + 2rem);
    align-self: start;
  }
  .chapter-number {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font: 0.8125rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);
    margin-block-end: 0.75rem;
  }
  .chapter-heading h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .chapter-heading p {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .chapter-content {
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }
  .chapter-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-block: 2.5rem 1rem;
  }
  .chapter-content > :first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }
  .chapter-content p {
    max-inline-size: 65ch;
  }
  .chapter-content p + p {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
  }
  .section-intro {
    margin-block-end: 1.75rem;
  }
  .example {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--color-footer-bg);
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }
  .statement-example {
    margin-block-end: 1.5rem;
  }
  .statement-example blockquote {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-weight: 400;
    max-inline-size: 28ch;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .statement-example figcaption {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .dark {
    background: #181713;
    color: #f3f3ed;
  }
  .dark a {
    color: #91adff;
  }
  .grid .example:not(.dark):has(.mark) {
    background: #fbfbfa;
    color: #25231f;
    border: 1px solid #ddddda;
  }
  .grid .example:not(.dark):has(.mark) a,
  .composition a {
    color: #1646d8;
  }
  .mark {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    margin-block: 2rem;
  }
  .example-caption {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .mono,
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .name-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    border-block: var(--rule-thin);
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .name-grid dt {
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font: 0.8125rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
  }
  .name-grid dd {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .table {
    inline-size: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    table-layout: fixed;
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .table th,
  .table td {
    text-align: start;
    vertical-align: top;
    border-block-end: var(--rule-thin);
    padding: 0.875rem 0.75rem 0.875rem 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .table thead th {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .table th:last-child,
  .table td:last-child {
    padding-inline-end: 0;
  }
  .specs th {
    inline-size: 35%;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-block-start: 0.625rem;
  }
  .caption {
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
  }
  .symbol-example {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .symbol-example > img {
    inline-size: 5rem;
    block-size: 5rem;
  }
  .symbol-sizes {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
  }
  .symbol-sizes figure {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
  .symbol-sizes img {
    margin: 0 auto 0.5rem;
  }
  .font-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    border-block-end: var(--rule-thin);
  }
  .family-use {
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  .font-sample {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .plex-sample {
    font: 400 1.5rem/1.3 var(--font-mono);
  }
  .colors {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .swatch {
    block-size: 6rem;
